    "solution": "Jump to the small upper lip beside the closed door and leave the echo there. Drop back through the gap to the freight bay and take the lantern. Board the carriage, shift toward its leading edge, and let it deliver you onto the plate. Jump and swap while its launch is still available: your departed echo keeps the plate pressed, and the carried lantern plus carriage lift return to the upper lip. Hold the launch rightward through the open door; the lantern shades the sunlight as you clear the long crossing. A delayed, stationary swap cannot reach the far landing, and leaving the lantern as the plate weight removes the needed shade.",
    "nearestExisting": "p131 The Citadel transfers a carriage launch to a high echo. p137 Onto the Plate swaps out of a sealed plate room. Here the departure location must remain physically occupied while cargo and launch travel together: using the lantern as a substitute plate weight removes the shade needed at the finish.",
    "novelty": "The same swap has three spatial consequences: where the gate weight remains, where the carried shade arrives, and which direction the knight is already moving. The high anchor has no cargo route back up, and a stationary swap leaves the carriage launch behind.",
